  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5347",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to CP50-MEL-B, suggesting a complex network of interactions. The first pathway links Mollicellin N to A704, which is targeted by palmarumycin CP18, and then to CP50-MEL-B. The second pathway connects Mollicellin N to P2X purinoceptor 1, which is targeted by a compound that also targets CP50-MEL-B. The third pathway links Mollicellin N to TE-9, which is targeted by the same compound as in the second pathway, also leading to CP50-MEL-B. These pathways collectively suggest that Mollicellin N may act through different molecular mechanisms, potentially targeting distinct receptors or pathways that ultimately converge on CP50-MEL-B. The evidence supports a role for Mollicellin N in modulating pathways that influence CP50-MEL-B, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
